            <ArticleTitle>Exercise simultaneously increases nasal patency and bronchial obstruction in asthmatic children.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1493-1495</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/resp.12849</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We found that simultaneous post-exercise increase in nasal patency and bronchial obstruction occurs only in children with atopic asthma, but not in sensitized children without asthma. In healthy children, the increase in nasal patency is accompanied by bronchial dilatation.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2016 Asian Pacific Society of Respirology.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
